WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
December 2008. Britain is in recession.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:07.470
The government cuts
VAT, a tax on spending,

3
00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:11.100
from 17.5 per cent to 15 per cent.

4
00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:15.020
The aim: to support spending
while the economy shrinks.

5
00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:16.190
Did it work?

6
00:00:16.190 --> 00:00:18.610
Economists still argue about it.

7
00:00:18.610 --> 00:00:20.420
So when a slump hits,

8
00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:23.000
can a government spend its way out of it?

9
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:26.140
In this mission, you'll shift
aggregate demand to close

10
00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:27.660
a gap in output.

11
00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.560
Then you'll use a graph lab:

12
00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:33.490
raise government spending
and see how far output moves.

13
00:00:33.490 --> 00:00:37.750
Your mission: find out what
fiscal policy can do in a slump,

14
00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:39.390
and what can hold it back.
